│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ k_shortest_paths_parallel_broadcast                                                       │
│ patch_description        │ The current algorithm routes every partition of every destination along a single Dijkstra │
│                          │ shortest path. This (1) concentrates all traffic on one path, causing                     │
│                          │ congestion/throughput bottlenecks, and (2) ignores parallel low-cost alternatives across  │
│                          │ multi-cloud networks. Improvement: for each (src, dst) pair, compute k shortest simple    │
│                          │ paths using `nx.shortest_simple_paths` (ranked by cumulative cost), then distribute the   │
│                          │ `num_partitions` across these paths using a greedy least-loaded assignment. This balances │
│                          │ load across networks, exploits parallel links, and lowers effective transfer cost by      │
│                          │ avoiding saturated high-throughput edges. Since partition paths may share edges with      │
│                          │ other destinations, we also track per-edge assigned partition counts and prefer paths     │
│                          │ minimizing (path_cost / available_paths) weighted by current edge load, reducing          │
│                          │ redundant heavy usage of the same links.                                                  │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
