│ patch_description        │ Crossover between the simple Dijkstra baseline and the k-path load-balancing version. The │
│                          │ current k-path version already improved total cost (1015.93 vs 1035.14), so I keep its    │
│                          │ multi-path exploration and edge-load tracking, but improve the partition assignment:      │
│                          │ instead of pure round-robin (which spreads partitions evenly across all k paths, even     │
│                          │ expensive ones), I use a weighted assignment that favors the cheapest path — the best     │
│                          │ path gets half the partitions, and the remainder are distributed over the next-best paths │
│                          │ to balance load. I also add caching of k-shortest-path candidates per destination and     │
│                          │ safe fallback to Dijkstra on errors, ensuring the program still runs on all configs.      │
