├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ multi_path_broadcast_share_relays                                                         │
│ patch_description        │ Current algorithm sends num_partitions copies along the single Dijkstra shortest path to  │
│                          │ each dst, causing redundant transfers. Improvement: for each partition, use a distinct    │
│                          │ k-shortest path (nx.shortest_simple_paths) so parallel network links are used and load is │
│                          │ spread. Also, partition-level routing via a shared relay tree reduces cost: instead of    │
│                          │ sending each partition per dst independently, send each partition once to a "relay" node  │
│                          │ that is closest (cost-wise) to all destinations, then fan out from the relay. Concretely, │
│                          │ for each partition j, compute a shortest path from src to a relay (chosen as the node     │
│                          │ minimizing sum of costs to dsts, approximated via multi-destination Dijkstra), and from   │
│                          │ the relay compute shortest paths to each dst. This reduces redundant transfers because    │
│                          │ the src->relay segment is shared across all destinations for that partition. This is a    │
│                          │ targeted change to search_algorithm.                                                      │
│ num_applied              │ 2                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0071                                                                                   │
