╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ load_aware_multi_path_broadcast                                                           │
│ patch_description        │ The current algorithm computes one shortest path per destination and assigns every        │
│                          │ partition to that same path. This overloads a single route (its per-edge throughput cap   │
│                          │ gets violated, driving costs up) and ignores cheaper parallel alternatives across         │
│                          │ networks. Improvement: for each destination, consider the K shortest simple paths (by     │
│                          │ cost), and distribute partitions across them in a load-balanced round-robin fashion. This │
│                          │ spreads flow over multiple egress links, keeps per-edge load under throughput             │
│                          │ constraints, and exploits low-cost parallel routes in multi-network topologies. We also   │
│                          │ remove a bug: incoming edges to src are removed from a graph copy, but edge metadata `G`  │
│                          │ is still fetched from the original G — keep that, but now compute candidate paths with an │
│                          │ effective-cost weight that penalizes congested edges so load balancing emerges naturally. │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0025                                                                                   │
│ error_attempt            │ None                                                                                      │
│ system_prompt_id         │ None                                                                                      │
