│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ dedup_shared_edges                                                                        │
│ patch_description        │ The key inefficiency is that each partition independently traverses the same edges from   │
│                          │ src, paying the same cost num_partitions times. Instead, assign each partition its own    │
│                          │ shortest path (shortest paths differ per partition by removing used edges), and for       │
│                          │ partitions that share a common prefix with the cheapest path, only re-send on diverging   │
│                          │ suffixes. The current code already scores candidates but the round-robin assignment       │
│                          │ ignores cost and still duplicates. Improve by: (1) computing per-partition distinct paths │
│                          │ via iterative edge-removal Dijkstra (k-shortest-path style), (2) preferring the absolute  │
│                          │ cheapest path for most partitions while spreading the remainder across parallel low-cost  │
│                          │ alternatives, and (3) keeping the load-balancing scoring. Also handle None costs          │
│                          │ gracefully (treat as excluded edges when possible paths exist).                           │
