│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ shared_edge_discount_dijkstra                                                             │
│ patch_description        │ The current algorithm computes a shortest path independently for each destination,        │
│                          │ ignoring that many destinations may share the same low-cost egress links. This causes     │
│                          │ redundant expensive transfers on parallel/identical routes. A better strategy: process    │
│                          │ destinations in order, and once an edge has been used by a previous destination's path,   │
│                          │ discount its effective cost (near zero) for subsequent route searches. This encourages    │
│                          │ later destinations to reuse already-paid-for links, producing a Steiner-tree-like         │
│                          │ broadcast structure that substantially reduces total transfer cost, while still           │
│                          │ guaranteeing each destination remains reachable. We use per-destination copies of the     │
│                          │ graph weights so the original graph G is untouched, and all num_partitions per            │
│                          │ destination are still populated exactly as before so the topology format stays            │
│                          │ compatible.                                                                               │
