│ patch_name               │ multicast_tree_broadcast_search                                                           │
│ patch_description        │ Restructure the search around a shared multicast routing layer instead of per-destination │
│                          │ independent shortest paths. A RoutePlanner first computes a low-cost shortest-path tree   │
│                          │ (Steiner-like) from the source, then spreads partitions across the tree edges and, when   │
│                          │ throughput capacity on a tree edge is exhausted, falls back to k-shortest alternative     │
│                          │ paths to balance load across networks. This reduces redundant transfers (shared segments  │
│                          │ carry multiple destinations' data once), avoids overloading cheap links (load balancing), │
│                          │ and keeps the same BroadCastTopology output format. The logic is split into modular       │
│                          │ components: RoutePlanner (path candidates + capacity tracking) and BroadcastPlanBuilder   │
│                          │ (fills BroadCastTopology), improving maintainability.                                     │
