│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ multi_path_load_balanced_broadcast                                                        │
│ patch_description        │ The current algorithm computes a single Dijkstra shortest path from src to each dst and   │
│                          │ assigns ALL partitions of that dst to the same path. This (1) overloads a single route    │
│                          │ with all num_partitions flows, and (2) ignores network diversity. A better strategy is to │
│                          │ compute k-shortest (lowest-cost) candidate paths per dst and spread partitions across     │
│                          │ those paths. To balance load across networks, we dynamically inflate the cost of edges as │
│                          │ they get used (congestion-aware pricing): each time an edge carries a partition, its      │
│                          │ effective cost is increased multiplicatively, so subsequent paths tend to reuse           │
│                          │ different, less-utilized links. This exploits multi-network topologies, reduces redundant │
│                          │ transfers over hot links, and spreads load, lowering overall cost and improving           │
│                          │ throughput feasibility. We use nx.shortest_simple_paths to get candidate paths in cost    │
│                          │ order, and assign partitions round-robin among the best candidates while tracking         │
│                          │ per-edge utilization.                                                                     │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
