│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ partition_edge_reuse_broadcast                                                            │
│ patch_description        │ Key parameters in prior approaches: congestion_factor (1.5, penalized load),              │
│                          │ max_candidates (4), and per-partition round-robin assignment. New configuration inverts   │
│                          │ the load penalty into a reuse reward: process destinations in decreasing                  │
│                          │ shortest-path-cost order and, per partition, select the candidate path maximizing         │
│                          │ (reuse_bonus * reused_edges - raw_cost). Parameters: reuse_bonus = 0.9 (fraction of cost  │
│                          │ credited back for each edge already used by an earlier destination in the same            │
│                          │ partition), max_candidates = num_partitions + 2, and a fallback alternation threshold of  │
│                          │ 15% cost increase to allow mild diversification when reuse offers no gain. Rationale: if  │
│                          │ cost is charged per unique edge (or with aggregate-flow discounts), reusing edges across  │
│                          │ destinations within a partition reduces total transfer cost while keeping the `[s, t, G]` │
│                          │ append format unchanged.                                                                  │
