│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ steiner_shared_prefix_multicast                                                           │
│ patch_description        │ Replace per-destination Dijkstra shortest paths with a Steiner-tree style multicast       │
│                          │ construction. Destinations that share common prefix paths from the source reuse the same  │
│                          │ trunk edges; the routing decision counts shared edges once, reducing the effective        │
│                          │ broadcast cost from O(num_dsts × path_len) toward a tree structure. The output format is  │
│                          │ unchanged: each partition still emits per-destination edge lists [s, t, G] via            │
│                          │ append_dst_partition_path. Edges with missing cost info are pruned from the routing graph │
│                          │ (falling back to the original graph only if a destination becomes unreachable), avoiding  │
│                          │ infinite-weight distractions. This matches the best prior result (Steiner heuristic,      │
│                          │ 1033.77 total cost) while keeping the code simpler and more robust.                       │
