│ patch_name               │ kshortest_loadaware_broadcast                                                             │
│ patch_description        │ Crossover of the k-shortest-simple-paths candidate pool (which gave the best cost,        │
│                          │ 1015.93) with the congestion-aware marginal-cost assignment from the Monte-Carlo variant. │
│                          │ For each destination we enumerate k cheap alternative simple paths (pruned to within a    │
│                          │ slack of the best), then assign partitions greedily by marginal cost: base edge cost      │
│                          │ scaled by a load-vs-throughput penalty, so partitions spread across parallel low-cost     │
│                          │ routes and avoid stacking on congested edges. This removes the expensive random sampling  │
│                          │ while retaining load balancing across networks.                                           │
