│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ joint_edge_reuse_broadcast                                                                │
│ patch_description        │ Restructure the solver into three stages: (1) graph preprocessing, (2) candidate route    │
│                          │ generation per destination (k shortest paths + load-aware Dijkstra re-runs), and (3) a    │
│                          │ joint cross-destination assignment pass. Destinations are processed in decreasing         │
│                          │ path-cost order, and for each partition the candidate path that reuses edges already      │
│                          │ committed for that same partition gets a reuse bonus (inverting the old load penalty into │
│                          │ a reward). If transfer cost is effectively charged per unique edge or aggregate flows are │
│                          │ discounted, this collapses traffic onto shared multicast-style trees and cuts redundant   │
│                          │ transfers, lowering total cost. Output format (`[s, t, G]` appends) is unchanged.         │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
