│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ cost_first_single_path                                                                    │
│ patch_description        │ The metrics show cost decreases monotonically as spreading is reduced: the load-aware     │
│                          │ spreading program (1005.13) is best so far, but earlier pure cost-first variants with     │
│                          │ less spreading got close (1035–1065). The recommendation is to go fully cost-first: for   │
│                          │ each destination, generate up to k=4 candidate paths via k-shortest-path enumeration      │
│                          │ (with Dijkstra fallback) and assign ALL partitions to the single cheapest path. Any       │
│                          │ spreading across parallel routes adds extra per-partition transfer cost without reducing  │
│                          │ total cost, so candidate generation is kept purely for robustness. This retains the       │
│                          │ structural advantages (k-shortest candidates, Dijkstra fallback, safe unreachable         │
│                          │ handling) while removing all load-based spreading that increased cost.                    │
