│                          │ process partitions in order and prefer candidate paths whose edges have already been used │
│                          │ by earlier partitions (or by previously processed destinations) — if cost is charged per  │
│                          │ unique edge or aggregate flows get discounted, reusing edges lowers total cost.           │
│                          │ Destinations are processed in decreasing shortest-path cost order so expensive            │
│                          │ destinations first establish the shared backbone that cheaper destinations can then       │
│                          │ piggyback on. Keeps the `[s, t, G]` append format untouched.                              │
