╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ iterated_reuse_discounting                                                                │
│ patch_description        │ Current approach splits partitions across pre-enumerated k paths, but never lets a later  │
│                          │ destination (or partition) "hitch a ride" on a trunk already paid for. Since all          │
│                          │ partitions originate at the same src, once a set of edges has been used, sending          │
│                          │ additional partitions/destinations over those edges adds (near) zero incremental cost.    │
│                          │ So: route each partition greedily with Dijkstra on a working copy of the graph whose edge │
│                          │ costs are discounted (to ~0) for edges already used in the current pass. Then add an      │
│                          │ outer refinement loop: re-run the whole routing pass with used_edges warm-started from    │
│                          │ the previous pass, keeping the pass with the lowest true (undiscounted) total cost. This  │
│                          │ encourages shared trunks across destinations and partitions, reduces redundant transfers, │
│                          │ and converges in 2-3 passes at trivial compute cost.                                      │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0093                                                                                   │
│ error_attempt            │ None                                                                                      │
│ system_prompt_id         │ None                                                                                      │
