│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ per_partition_edge_dedup_steiner                                                          │
│ patch_description        │ The prior programs (and current one) append the *full* src→dst path to every partition    │
│                          │ for every destination, so shared trunk edges get billed once per destination per          │
│                          │ partition — wasting all the sharing the Steiner-style construction creates (insight from  │
│                          │ Gen 11/16/19). The fix: build the shared trunk once via the shortest-path Steiner         │
│                          │ heuristic, record each destination's full root-to-terminal path, and then emit edges per  │
│                          │ partition with explicit deduplication — each edge of a partition is emitted exactly once, │
│                          │ attributed to the first destination whose path uses it. Since all destinations' paths     │
│                          │ form one tree, each partition ends up carrying exactly one copy of the whole Steiner tree │
│                          │ instead of num_dsts overlapping copies. This directly targets the deduplication the       │
│                          │ cost_score gap implies while keeping the output format `[s, t, G]` and the per-(dst,      │
│                          │ partition) structure intact.                                                              │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0155                                                                                   │
