│ patch_description        │ Extends the current multi-pass Steiner-like approach with a throughput feasibility check  │
│                          │ on heavily-shared trunk edges. In `route_pass`, we track how many destinations route over │
│                          │ each edge; once aggregate demand (dest_count × per-dst flow) exceeds the edge's           │
│                          │ throughput, we restore the original cost for subsequent Dijkstra runs so later            │
│                          │ destinations route around the saturated edge. This prevents silent capacity violations    │
│                          │ that gate cost_score. Per prior evidence, throughput is used only as a hard feasibility   │
│                          │ filter, never as load-spreading (which cost 5–10%). We keep the candidate-ordering search │
│                          │ and refinement passes, but pass per-dst flow (estimated as num_partitions) into the       │
│                          │ feasibility check.                                                                        │
