│ patch_description        │ Crossover of the best-performing variant (reuse-discounted refinement loop, total cost    │
│                          │ 756.69) with the k-candidate path enumeration from the inspiration program. Key           │
│                          │ improvements: (1) for each destination, enumerate up to k shortest simple paths on the    │
│                          │ discounted graph and pick the one minimizing *incremental* cost (edges already paid for   │
│                          │ by other destinations/partitions are heavily discounted, encouraging shared broadcast     │
│                          │ trunks); (2) all partitions of a destination follow the selected consolidated route to    │
│                          │ avoid paying for multiple parallel trunks; (3) multiple refinement passes with escalating │
│                          │ discounts (0.0, 0.25, 0.5) reuse edges discovered in earlier passes, and the final        │
│                          │ topology is chosen as the one with the lowest undiscounted total cost, guaranteeing we    │
│                          │ never regress versus the plain-Dijkstra baseline.                                         │
